# Copy this file to .env.local for local development.
#
# .env.local is git-ignored. Never commit a populated copy of this file.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- database

# The connection CORSC's API uses. On Supabase this is the pooled connection
# string. The role it names must be able to bypass row-level security — see
# docs/DATABASE.md, "Two access paths, two controls". On Supabase the `postgres`
# role already can.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/corsc

# The unpooled connection, used only by `prisma migrate`. Migrations cannot run
# through a transaction pooler. On a plain PostgreSQL this is the same value as
# DATABASE_URL.
DIRECT_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/corsc

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- auth
#
# Both values below are PUBLIC by design: they are shipped to the browser in the
# client bundle, so they are not secrets and cannot be treated as an access
# control. What protects patient data on the direct-to-database path is
# row-level security; what protects it on the API path is the authorisation in
# lib/backend/auth.ts.
#
# Consequences, which matter for a clinical deployment:
#   - Publishing the publishable key is safe ONLY while RLS is enabled on every
#     table holding patient data. Verify this before any real patient data is
#     entered. tests/database/schema.test.ts asserts it.
#   - The service-role key must never appear in this file, in any NEXT_PUBLIC_
#     variable, or anywhere in the client bundle. It bypasses RLS entirely.
#     CORSC does not read it: nothing under lib/backend requires it, and adding
#     a dependency on it would be a regression.
#
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_your_key_here

# --------------------------------------------------------------- optional

# Set by CI so that a skipped database test suite fails the build instead of
# reporting green. Leave unset locally.
# CORSC_REQUIRE_DB=1

# The formulary import reads these CSVs from the repository root.
# CORSC_INGREDIENTS_CSV=ingredients 2.0.csv
# CORSC_PRODUCTS_CSV=products 2.0.csv
